<title>HUNGARY: IBM HUNGARY SEEN TO FLY 2,000 T/YR TO U.S..</title>
<headline>IBM HUNGARY SEEN TO FLY 2,000 T/YR TO U.S..</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Business Machines Corp (IBM) plans to send roughly 2,000 tonnes a year of computer and electronic parts from its Hungarian plants by air to the United States, with shipments starting by 1998, cargo industry sources in Budapest told Reuters.</p>
<p>IBM is expected before September to name a freight forwarder to handle the shipments, but it was not clear when this year the deliveries would start, the sources said.</p>
<p>IBM already sends roughly 4,000 tonnes a year of parts and raw material by air from the Far East to major airports in western Europe for delivery by truck into Hungary, the sources said.</p>
<p>-- Ryan Tutak, Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
